From: radiance-web EnergyPlus WASM port
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] third_party/fmt-8.0.1: de-space user-defined-literal operators

What: `operator"" _a` -> `operator""_a` and `operator"" _format` -> `operator""_format`
(4 sites total: 2 in format.h, 2 in xchar.h; this file covers format.h's 2 sites,
see 0003 for xchar.h's 2 sites).

Why (toolchain, not physics): a space between the `""` and the literal-operator
suffix was legal but deprecated C++11/14 syntax for user-defined-literal
declarators. clang >= 23 (Emscripten's bundled compiler) promotes the
deprecation to a hard error under fmt 8.0.1's warning/pedantic settings. This is
a tokenization-only change in the declarator spelling -- the operator's name,
signature, and runtime behavior are unchanged.

Applies to: energyplus-src/third_party/fmt-8.0.1/include/fmt/format.h
Apply with (-p1, from the pristine energyplus-src/ tree root):
  patch -p1 < patches/energyplus/0002-fmt8-udl-format-h.patch

--- a/third_party/fmt-8.0.1/include/fmt/format.h
+++ b/third_party/fmt-8.0.1/include/fmt/format.h
@@ -2867,7 +2867,7 @@
   return {};
 }
 #  else
-constexpr auto operator"" _a(const char* s, size_t) -> detail::udl_arg<char> {
+constexpr auto operator""_a(const char* s, size_t) -> detail::udl_arg<char> {
   return {s};
 }
 #  endif
@@ -2882,7 +2882,7 @@
     std::string message = "The answer is {}"_format(42);
   \endrst
  */
-constexpr auto operator"" _format(const char* s, size_t n)
+constexpr auto operator""_format(const char* s, size_t n)
     -> detail::udl_formatter<char> {
   return {{s, n}};
 }
